#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:118
msgid "Exercise 2: My first metadynamics simulation"
msgstr "演習2：初めての Metadynamics"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:120
msgid ""
"In this exercise we will setup and perform a well-tempered metadynamics run "
"using the backbone dihedral $\\phi$ as collective variable. During the "
"calculation, we will also monitor the behavior of the other backbone "
"dihedral $\\psi$. Here you can find a sample `plumed.dat` file that you can "
"use as a template."
msgstr ""
"Backbone Dihedral $\\phi$ を CV とする Well-tempered Metadynamics "
"を設定・実行します。もう一方の Backbone Dihedral $\\psi$ も監視します。次の `plumed.dat` をひな形に使えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:147
msgid ""
"Once your `plumed.dat` file is complete, you can run a 20 ns long "
"metadynamics simulations starting from either of the two provided "
"conformations, for example `topolA.tpr`. All you need to do is execute the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""
"`plumed.dat` が完成したら、例えば `topolA.tpr` など、付属のいずれかの構造から20 ns 実行します。次のコマンドを使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:153
msgid ""
"During the metadynamics simulation, PLUMED will create two files, named "
"`COLVAR` and `HILLS`. The `COLVAR` file contains all the information "
"specified by the PRINT command, in this case the value of the backbone "
"dihedrals $\\phi$ and $\\psi$ every 10 steps of simulation. The `HILLS` file"
" contains a list of the Gaussian kernels deposited along the simulation."
msgstr ""
"PLUMED は `COLVAR` と `HILLS` を作ります。`COLVAR` は PRINT の指定内容、ここでは10 Step ごとの "
"$\\phi$ と $\\psi$ です。`HILLS` はシミュレーション中に追加した Gaussian Kernel の一覧です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:155
msgid ""
"Let's visualize the time series of the two collective variables. Take your "
"time to inspect the behavior of the two CVs. __What are the main differences"
" with respect to the trajectories you produced from the first exercise?__"
msgstr "両 CV の時系列を可視化し、挙動をよく調べてください。__演習1の Trajectory との主な違いは何ですか？__"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:157
msgid ""
"At this point, we can estimate the free energy as a function of the "
"metadynamics CV directly from the metadynamics bias potential. In order to "
"do so, the utility sum_hills can be used to sum the Gaussian kernels "
"deposited during the simulation and stored in the `HILLS` file. To calculate"
" the free energy as a function of $\\phi$, it is sufficient to use the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""
"BiasPotential から Metadynamics CV の関数として自由エネルギーを直接推定できます。sum_hills は `HILLS` "
"の Gaussian Kernel を足し合わせます。$\\phi$ の関数として求めるには、次を使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:163
msgid ""
"The command above generates a file called `fes.dat` in which the free-energy"
" surface as function of $\\phi$ is calculated on a regular grid. One can "
"modify the default name for the free-energy file, as well as the boundaries "
"and bin size of the grid, by using the following sum_hills options:"
msgstr ""
"`fes.dat` に $\\phi$ の自由エネルギー表面を等間隔 Grid で出力します。ファイル名、Grid の境界、Bin 幅は "
"sum_hills の次のオプションで変えられます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:173
msgid ""
"To give a preliminary assessment of the convergence of a metadynamics "
"simulation, one can calculate the estimate of the free energy as a function "
"of simulation time. At convergence, the reconstructed profiles should be "
"similar. The sum_hills option `--stride` should be used to give an estimate "
"of the free energy every `N` Gaussian kernels deposited, and the option "
"`--mintozero` can be used to align the profiles by setting the global "
"minimum to zero. If we use the following command:"
msgstr ""
"収束の予備評価には、各時刻の自由エネルギー推定を比較します。収束時には Profile が似るはずです。`--stride` で `N` "
"Gaussian ごとに計算し、`--mintozero` で大域的最小を0に揃えます。次の場合は、"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:179
msgid ""
"one free energy is calculated every 200 Gaussian kernels deposited, and the "
"global minimum is set to zero in all profiles. Now, you can visualize the "
"free-energy estimate as a function of simulation time and assess how it "
"changed during the course of the simulation. In the last part of this 20 ns "
"long metadynamics simulation, the free-energy estimate should not change "
"significantly."
msgstr ""
"200 Gaussian ごとに自由エネルギーを求め、全 Profile "
"の最小を0にします。時間とともに推定がどう変わるか可視化・評価してください。20 ns の後半では、大きく変わらないはずです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:181
msgid ""
"Looking at the time-evolution of the entire free-energy profile might not be"
" straightforward. Therefore, what we usually do is focusing on a few "
"metastable states, or local free-energy minima, and calculating their "
"estimated free-energy difference as a function of time. In case of alanine "
"dipeptide, this is rather easy since there are only two major states in the "
"free-energy profile as a function of the CV $\\phi$."
msgstr ""
"Profile 全体の時間発展は把握しにくいため、通常は少数の準安定状態、すなわち局所自由エネルギー極小の間の差に注目します。Alanine "
"Dipeptide の $\\phi$ の Profile には主要状態が2つだけなので簡単です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:183
msgid "The users should now:"
msgstr "次を行ってください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:185
msgid ""
"calculate from the estimate of the free energy $F(\\phi)$ at a given "
"simulation time, the difference in free energy between the two basins. In "
"order to do this, you should define a reasonable interval around the two "
"local free-energy minima and recall that the probability of this state is "
"the integral of the probability $P(\\phi)= exp(-F(\\phi)/k_BT)$ in the "
"chosen interval;"
msgstr ""
"各時刻の $F(\\phi)$ から2 Basin の自由エネルギー差を計算する。各局所極小の周囲に妥当な区間を定め、状態確率はその区間での "
"$P(\\phi)= exp(-F(\\phi)/k_BT)$ の積分であることを使う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:186
msgid ""
"plot the estimated free-energy difference as a function of simulation time."
msgstr "推定した自由エネルギー差を時間に対して描画する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:188
msgid "These two observations:"
msgstr "次の2つの観測は、"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:189
msgid "the system is diffusing rapidly in the entire CV space"
msgstr "系が CV 空間全体を速やかに拡散する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:190
msgid ""
"the estimated free energy does not significantly change as a function of "
"time"
msgstr "推定自由エネルギーが時間とともに大きく変わらない。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:192
msgid "are two indications that the simulation __might__ have converged."
msgstr "収束した __可能性__ を示します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:194
msgid ""
"__IMPORTANT: The two conditions listed above are necessary, but not "
"sufficient to declare convergence. We will learn below how to perform a "
"quantitative analysis of the convergence of a metadynamics simulation.__"
msgstr "__重要：上の2条件は収束の必要条件ですが、十分条件ではありません。後で定量的な収束解析を学びます。__"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:196
msgid "Exercise 3: Reweighting (unbiasing) a metadynamics simulation"
msgstr "演習3：Metadynamics の Reweighting（Bias の除去）"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:198
msgid ""
"In the previous exercise we biased $\\phi$ and computed the free energy as a"
" function of the same variable directly from the metadynamics bias potential"
" using the sum_hills utility. However, in many cases you might decide which "
"variable should be analyzed _after_ having performed a metadynamics "
"simulation. For example, you might want to calculate the free energy as a "
"function of CVs other than those biased during the metadynamics simulation, "
"such as the dihedral $\\psi$. At variance with standard MD simulations, you "
"cannot simply calculate histograms of other variables directly from your "
"metadynamics trajectory, because the presence of the metadynamics bias "
"potential has altered the statistical weight of each frame. To remove the "
"effect of this bias and thus be able to calculate properties of the system "
"in the unbiased ensemble, you must reweight (unbias) your simulation."
msgstr ""
"前の演習では $\\phi$ に Bias を加え、sum_hills で同じ変数の自由エネルギーを BiasPotential "
"から求めました。ただし解析変数を _実行後に_ 選びたいこともあります。例えば Bias を加えていない Dihedral $\\psi$ "
"の自由エネルギーです。通常 MD と違い、Metadynamics Trajectory の別変数の Histogram "
"をそのまま計算できません。BiasPotential が Frame の統計的重みを変えたためです。Unbiased Ensemble "
"の性質を求めるには Reweighting で Bias を除きます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:201
msgid ""
"There are multiple ways to calculate the correct statistical weight of each "
"frame in your metadynamics trajectory and thus to reweight your simulation. "
"For example:"
msgstr "各 Frame の正しい統計的重みを求める方法は複数あります。例えば、"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:203
msgid ""
"weights can be calculated by considering the time-dependence of the "
"metadynamics bias potential as discussed in [this "
"paper](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/jp504920s)."
msgstr ""
"[この論文](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/jp504920s) のように BiasPotential "
"の時間依存性を考慮する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:204
msgid ""
"weights can be calculated using the metadynamics bias potential obtained at "
"the end of the simulation and assuming a constant bias during the entire "
"course of the simulation as discussed in [this "
"paper](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/ct3002464)."
msgstr ""
"[この論文](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/ct3002464) のように、終了時の BiasPotential "
"が全期間で一定だったと仮定する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:206
msgid ""
"In this exercise we will use the second method, which is identical to the "
"umbrella-sampling reweighting approach that you may have come across in "
"other masterclasses. In order to compute the weights we will use the driver "
"tool."
msgstr ""
"ここでは2番目を使います。ほかの Masterclass の Umbrella Sampling の Reweighting と同じです。重みは "
"driver で計算します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:208
msgid ""
"First of all, you need to prepare a `plumed_reweight.dat` file that is "
"identical to the one you used for running your metadynamics simulation "
"except for a few modifications:"
msgstr "実行時の入力を基に `plumed_reweight.dat` を作り、次を変更します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:210
msgid ""
"you need to add the keyword `RESTART=YES` to the METAD command. This will "
"make this action behave as if PLUMED was restarting, i.e. PLUMED will read "
"from the `HILLS` file the Gaussians that have previously been accumulated;"
msgstr ""
"METAD に `RESTART=YES` を加える。PLUMED が再開時と同様に `HILLS` の蓄積済み Gaussian を読み込む。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:211
msgid ""
"you need to set the Gaussian `HEIGHT` to zero and the `PACE` to a large "
"number. This will actually avoid adding new Gaussians (and even if they are "
"added they will have zero height);"
msgstr ""
"Gaussian の `HEIGHT` を0、`PACE` を大きな数にする。新しい Gaussian をほぼ追加せず、追加されても高さは0になる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:212
msgid ""
"you need to modify the PRINT statement so that you write every frame and "
"that, in addition to `phi` and `psi`, you also write `metad.bias`;"
msgstr "PRINT を変更し、全 Frame で `phi`、`psi` に加えて `metad.bias` も出力する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:213
msgid ""
"you might also want to change the name of the output file to "
"`COLVAR_REWEIGHT`."
msgstr "出力名を `COLVAR_REWEIGHT` に変えてもよい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:215
msgid "Here how the `plumed_reweight.dat` should look like:"
msgstr "`plumed_reweight.dat` は次のようになります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:242
msgid "Now you can run the driver tool using this command:"
msgstr "次で driver を実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:248
msgid ""
"where `traj_comp.xtc` is the metadynamics trajectory produced in exercise 2."
" Notice that you have to specify the value of $k_BT$ in energy units. While "
"running your simulation this information was communicated by the MD code."
msgstr ""
"`traj_comp.xtc` は演習2の Trajectory です。エネルギー単位で $k_BT$ を指定する必要があります。MD "
"実行中は、この情報は MD コードから渡されていました。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:250
msgid ""
"As a result, PLUMED will produce a new `COLVAR_REWEIGHT` file with one "
"additional column containing the metadynamics bias potential $V(s)$ "
"calculated using all the Gaussians deposited along the entire trajectory. "
"You can easily obtain the weight $w$ of each frame using the expression "
"$w\\propto\\exp\\left(\\frac{V(s)}{k_BT}\\right)$ (umbrella-sampling-like "
"reweighting). At this point, you can read the `COLVAR_REWEIGHT` file using a"
" python notebook and compute a weighted histogram or, alternatively, if you "
"want PLUMED to do the weighted histograms for you, you can add the following"
" lines at the end of the `plumed_reweight.dat` file and re-run PLUMED "
"driver:"
msgstr ""
"新しい `COLVAR_REWEIGHT` に、全 Gaussian から計算した BiasPotential $V(s)$ の列が追加されます。各 "
"Frame の重み $w$ は $w\\propto\\exp\\left(\\frac{V(s)}{k_BT}\\right)$ "
"で求められます（Umbrella Sampling 型 Reweighting）。Python Notebook で `COLVAR_REWEIGHT`"
" を読み、Weighted Histogram を計算できます。PLUMED に計算させるなら、`plumed_reweight.dat` "
"の末尾に次を加え、driver を再実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:272
msgid ""
"You can now compare the free energies as a function of $\\phi$ calculated:"
msgstr "$\\phi$ の自由エネルギーを、次の方法間で比較してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:274
msgid ""
"directly from the metadynamics bias potential using sum_hills as done in "
"exercise 2;"
msgstr "演習2の sum_hills による BiasPotential からの直接計算。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:275
msgid "using the reweighting procedure introduced in this exercise."
msgstr "この演習の Reweighting。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:277
msgid "__Are the two free energies identical?__"
msgstr "__2つの自由エネルギーは同じですか？__"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:280
msgid "Exercise 4: Estimating the error in free energies using block-analysis"
msgstr "演習4：Block Analysis による自由エネルギー誤差の推定"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:282
msgid ""
"In the previous exercise, we calculated the _final_ bias $V(s)$ on the "
"entire metadynamics trajectory and we used this quantity to calculate the "
"correct statistical weight of each frame, which is needed to reweight the "
"biased simulation. In this exercise, the user will learn how this "
"information can be used to calculate the error in the reconstructed free "
"energies and assess whether the simulation is converged or not."
msgstr ""
"前の演習では、_最終_ Bias $V(s)$ を全 Trajectory で評価し、Reweighting に必要な各 Frame "
"の重みを求めました。ここでは、それを使って自由エネルギーの誤差を計算し、収束を評価します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:284
msgid "Let's first:"
msgstr "まず次を行います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:286
msgid ""
"calculate the un-biasing weights "
"$w\\propto\\exp\\left(\\frac{V(s)}{k_BT}\\right)$ from the `COLVAR_REWEIGHT`"
" file obtained at the end of exercise 3;"
msgstr ""
"演習3の `COLVAR_REWEIGHT` から $w\\propto\\exp\\left(\\frac{V(s)}{k_BT}\\right)$ "
"を計算する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:287
msgid ""
"print them in a file (called for example `phi.weight`) containing the value "
"of the dihedral $\\phi$ and the corresponding (un-normalized) weight $w$ for"
" each frame of the metadynamics trajectory."
msgstr "各 Frame の $\\phi$ と対応する未正規化の重み $w$ を、例えば `phi.weight` に出力する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:289
msgid ""
"At this point we can apply the block-analysis technique (for more info about"
" the theory, have a look at other masterclasses) to calculate the average "
"free energy across the blocks and the error as a function of block size. For"
" your convenience, the `do_block_fes.py` python script provided in the "
"`data` directory of the `GitHub` repository of this Masterclass can be used "
"to read the `phi.weight` file and produce the desired output. The users "
"should properly choose the following input parameters:"
msgstr ""
"Block Analysis で Block 間の平均自由エネルギーと、Block Size ごとの誤差を計算します。理論はほかの "
"Masterclass を参照してください。`GitHub` の `data` にある Python スクリプト `do_block_fes.py` "
"が、`phi.weight` を読み込んで必要な出力を生成します。次の入力パラメータを適切に選んでください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:303
msgid ""
"and run the above script for different block sizes ranging from 1 to 1000. "
"For each choice of block size, the script will produce an output file, which"
" contains 3 colums:"
msgstr "Block Size を1〜1000に変えて実行します。各 Size で3列の出力が生成されます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:305
msgid "the value of the $\\phi$ variable on a grid;"
msgstr "Grid 上の $\\phi$ の値。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:306
msgid "the free energy averaged across the blocks for each point of the grid;"
msgstr "各 Grid 点の Block 間平均自由エネルギー。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:307
msgid "the associated error for each point of the grid."
msgstr "各 Grid 点の対応する誤差。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:309
msgid "At this point, the users should:"
msgstr "次を行ってください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:311
msgid ""
"calculate the average error across the free-energy profile, i.e. the grid "
"points, for each block size chosen;"
msgstr "各 Block Size について、自由エネルギー Profile の全 Grid 点で平均誤差を計算する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:312
msgid "visualize this average error as a function of the block size."
msgstr "平均誤差を Block Size に対して描画する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:314
msgid ""
"The users should verify that the error increases with the block size (why?) "
"until it reaches a plateau when the dimension of the block exceeds the "
"correlation time between data points. If a plateau is not observed, then the"
" simulation is not converged yet and should be run a bit longer."
msgstr ""
"Block Size とともに誤差が増え（なぜでしょうか？）、データの Correlation Time を超えると Plateau "
"に達することを確認します。Plateau がなければ未収束で、長く実行する必要があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:318
msgid ""
"__From this analysis, what can we say about the convergence of the "
"metadynamics simulation performed in exercise 2?__"
msgstr "__この解析から、演習2の Metadynamics の収束について何がいえますか？__"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:320
msgid "Exercise 5: Recognizing good from bad CVs"
msgstr "演習5：よい CV と悪い CV の見分け方"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:322
msgid ""
"In the previous exercises, we have performed a metadynamics simulation on "
"alanine dipeptide using the backbone dihedral $\\phi$ as CV. We have "
"analyzed the simulation and noticed that:"
msgstr ""
"ここまで Alanine Dipeptide の Backbone Dihedral $\\phi$ を CV とする Metadynamics "
"を行い、次を確認しました。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:324
msgid ""
"under the effect of the bias potential, the system rapidly diffuses in the "
"entire CV space;"
msgstr "BiasPotential により CV 空間全体を速く拡散する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:325
msgid ""
"the error in the reconstructed free energy calculated with block analysis "
"rapidly reaches a plateau."
msgstr "Block Analysis による自由エネルギー誤差が速やかに Plateau に達する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:327
msgid ""
"These two observations indicate that our simulation is converged and that "
"the dihedral $\\phi$ can be considered a _good_ CV. A good set of CVs for "
"metadynamics should:"
msgstr ""
"この2点から、収束し、Dihedral $\\phi$ が _よい_ CV であるといえます。Metadynamics のよい CV "
"集合は、次を満たします。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:329
msgid "discriminate between the relevant metastable states of the system;"
msgstr "重要な準安定状態を識別する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:330
msgid ""
"include all the slow modes that characterize transitions between such "
"states;"
msgstr "状態間遷移を特徴付けるすべての Slow Mode を含む。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:331
msgid "be as small as possible."
msgstr "数ができる限り少ない。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:333
msgid ""
"Identifying a priori a good set of CVs to describe a specific problem is far"
" from trivial. In this exercise, the users will learn how to detect "
"potential problems in their choice of CV(s). Let's first perform additional "
"1D metadynamics simulations using one of the following CVs:"
msgstr ""
"よい CV を事前に特定するのは容易ではありません。ここでは CV 選択の問題を検出する方法を学びます。まず次のいずれかで追加の1次元 "
"Metadynamics を行います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:335
msgid "the dihedral $\\psi$;"
msgstr "Dihedral $\\psi$。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:336
msgid "the radius of gyration, defined on all the heavy atoms of the system;"
msgstr "全 Heavy Atom の Radius of Gyration。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:337
msgid "the distance between Oxigen atom 6 and Hydrogen atom 8."
msgstr "酸素原子6と水素原子8の距離。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:339
msgid ""
"The users are invited to prepare, for each of the CV listed above, a PLUMED "
"input file to perform a 1D well-tempered metadynamics simulation, execute "
"the simulation, and analyse the results in terms of:"
msgstr "各 CV の1次元 Well-tempered Metadynamics 用 PLUMED 入力を作成して実行し、次を解析してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:341
msgid "diffusion of the system in the space of the dihedral $\\phi$"
msgstr "Dihedral $\\phi$ 空間での拡散。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:342
msgid "error analysis in the free energy as a function of $\\phi$"
msgstr "$\\phi$ の関数としての自由エネルギーの誤差。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:344
msgid ""
"and compare the results with the previous simulation in which $\\phi$ was "
"used as the metadynamics CV. __Based on this analysis, can you discriminate "
"between _good_ from _bad_ CVs?__"
msgstr "前の $\\phi$ を CV とする結果と比較してください。__解析から _よい_ CV と _悪い_ CV を見分けられますか？__"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:346
msgid ""
"To complete this exercise, the users should define and test a new CV that is"
" either:"
msgstr "最後に、次のいずれかの新しい CV を定義してテストしてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:348
msgid "as good as the dihedral $\\phi$;"
msgstr "Dihedral $\\phi$ と同程度によい CV。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:349
msgid ""
"the worst possible CV to accelerate sampling and describe the two main "
"conformational states of alanine dipeptide."
msgstr "Alanine Dipeptide の主要2状態を記述し Sampling を加速する上で、最も悪い CV。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:351 INSTRUCTIONS.md:391
msgid "__Please post the results of your simulations on Slack!__"
msgstr "__シミュレーション結果を Slack に投稿してください！__"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:353
msgid "Exercise 6: A 'real-life' application"
msgstr "演習6：実際の応用"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:355
msgid ""
"In this last exercise, we will tackle a real-life biological problem: "
"studying the conformational transition of a complex biological system. The "
"system that we are going to study is the C-terminal domain (CTD) of the RfaH"
" virulence factor from _Escherichia coli_. As shown in the figure below, "
"this part of the system, which we refer to as RfaH-CTD, undergoes a dramatic"
" conformational transformation from β-barrel to α-helical, which is "
"stabilized by the N-terminal domain of the RfaH virulence factor."
msgstr ""
"最後に、複雑な生物系の Conformational Transition を調べます。系は _Escherichia coli_ の病原性因子 "
"RfaH の C-terminal Domain (CTD)、RfaH-CTD です。下図のように β-barrel から α-helix "
"への大きな変換を起こし、α-helix は RfaH の N-terminal Domain に安定化されます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:357
msgid ""
"![Structural transformation of the RfaH-CTD. Domain dissociation is "
"triggered upon binding of the NTD (gray) to its target ops (operon polarity "
"suppressor) element DNA, relieving the autoinhibited state and allowing the "
"transformation of the CTD (colored) from an α-helical hairpin (A) towards a "
"five-stranded β-barrel (B). Note that the NTD and CTD are connected by a "
"linker that does not order within the crystals and therefore is not shown in"
" the figure.](figures/RfaH-CTD.png)"
msgstr ""
"![RfaH-CTD の構造変化。NTD（灰色）が標的の ops（Operon Polarity Suppressor）DNA Element "
"に結合すると、Domain の Dissociation が起きる。Autoinhibited State が解除され、CTD（色付き）は "
"α-Helical Hairpin（A）から5本鎖の β-Barrel（B）へ変化できる。NTD と CTD をつなぐ Linker "
"は結晶中で秩序化しないため、図には示していない。](figures/RfaH-CTD.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:359
msgid ""
"In the `data/RfaH-CTD` folder of the `GitHub` repository of this "
"Masterclass, you will find:"
msgstr "`GitHub` の `data/RfaH-CTD` に、次があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:361
msgid "two PDB files of RfaH-CTD in the α-helical and β-barrel states;"
msgstr "α-helix、β-barrel 状態の RfaH-CTD の2つの PDB。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:362
msgid ""
"a `topol.tpr` file, which is needed to perform a MD simulation of this sytem"
" with GROMACS."
msgstr "GROMACS で実行するための `topol.tpr`。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:364
msgid "The objective of this exercises are to:"
msgstr "目的は次のとおりです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:366
msgid ""
"compute the free-energy difference between the α-helical and β-barrel states"
" of RfaH-CTD (with error estimate);"
msgstr "RfaH-CTD の α-helix と β-barrel の自由エネルギー差を誤差付きで求める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:367
msgid ""
"(optional) determine the structure and population of other metastable "
"states, if present."
msgstr "任意：ほかの準安定状態があれば、構造と Population を求める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:369
msgid "In order to complete the exercise, the students should:"
msgstr "次を行ってください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:371
msgid ""
"choose their own CVs (maximum 3) and perform a well-tempered metadynamics "
"simulation. Any CV natively implemented in PLUMED (see "
"[here](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-doc/html/colvarintro.html)) or"
" defined by the users directly in the input file (see "
"[CUSTOM](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-doc/html/_c_u_s_t_o_m.html))"
" can be used;"
msgstr ""
"自分で最大3つの CV を選び、Well-tempered Metadynamics を行う。PLUMED に [実装済みの "
"CV](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-doc/html/colvarintro.html) "
"も、[CUSTOM](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/_c_u_s_t_o_m.html) で入力に直接定義する CV も使える。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:372
msgid ""
"monitor the RMSD of the system from the two reference conformations during "
"the course of the simulation;"
msgstr "実行中、2つの参照 Conformation に対する RMSD を監視する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:373
msgid ""
"analyze the results as done in the previous exercises (assessment of "
"convergence and error analysis);"
msgstr "前の演習と同様に収束と誤差を解析する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:374
msgid ""
"report the free energies (with error bar) as a function of the two RMSD CVs "
"calculated with respect to the reference PDBs;"
msgstr "参照 PDB に対する2つの RMSD CV の関数として、自由エネルギーを Error Bar 付きで報告する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:375
msgid ""
"(optional) report structure and population of the most signicant, i.e. "
"populated, states."
msgstr "任意：Population が大きい主要状態の構造と Population を報告する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:377
msgid "Please keep in mind that:"
msgstr "次の点に注意してほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:379
msgid ""
"we are simulating the system using a simplified, structure-based potential, "
"called [SMOG](https://smog-server.org). SMOG is significantly less "
"computational demanding than all-atoms, explicit solvent force fields. "
"However, the simulation of this system might take a few hours, so allocate "
"enough time to complete this exercise;"
msgstr ""
"[SMOG](https://smog-server.org) という簡略化した Structure-based Potential "
"を使います。All-atom Explicit Solvent Force Field "
"より計算コストは大幅に低いですが、数時間かかる場合があるので時間を確保してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:380
msgid ""
"some of the CVs or PLUMED functionalities might not work as hydrogen atoms "
"are not present in the system. However, there is always a way around this, "
"so be creative;"
msgstr "水素がないため一部の CV・PLUMED 機能は動かない場合がありますが、工夫して回避できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:381
msgid ""
"due to the nature of the force field, we are simulating at an unphysical "
"temperature of 60K. Be ready to test large values of the `BIASFACTOR`."
msgstr "Force Field の特性から、非物理的な60 K で実行します。`BIASFACTOR` は大きな値も試してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:383
msgid ""
"Finally, due to the special nature of the force field, please execute "
"GROMACS using the following command:"
msgstr "Force Field が特殊なので、GROMACS は次のコマンドで実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:389
msgid ""
"You can adjust the number of CPU cores you want to use (here 4, OpenMP "
"parallelization), based on the available resources. The system is not "
"particularly big, therefore using a large number of cores might be "
"inefficient."
msgstr ""
"資源に応じて CPU Core 数（ここでは4、OpenMP 並列化）を調整できます。系は大きくないため、多数の Core は非効率な場合があります。"
